{"metric":"white_hole","source":[{"metric":"white_hole","system":"exterior_eddington_finkelstein","fields":["coords","inverse_metric_components","metric_components","parameters"],"version":"2258c3f7221a726a"},{"metric":"white_hole","system":"exterior_kruskal","fields":["coords","inverse_metric_components","metric_components","parameters"],"version":"52ba19c17fd41bd3"},{"metric":"white_hole","system":"exterior_schwarzschild","fields":["coords","inverse_metric_components","kretschmann","metric_components","parameters"],"version":"92b471a878039a34"},{"metric":"white_hole","system":"interior_comoving","fields":["coords","inverse_metric_components","kretschmann","metric_components","parameters"],"version":"863f6c0b724cba1e"},{"metric":"white_hole","system":"interior_conformal","fields":["coords","inverse_metric_components","metric_components","parameters"],"version":"15836ffeb9d956e3"}],"views":[{"id":"burst","label":"Interior and exterior","box":[-0.35,5.8478,-3.4416,3.4416],"settings":"$R_0 = 2\\,r_s$, so that $\\chi_0 = \\pi/4$ and $a_m = 2\\sqrt{2}\\,r_s$; the dust leaves its singularity at $\\eta = 0$, is at rest at $\\eta = \\pi$, the line $T = 0$, and falls back to $\\eta = 2\\pi$.","caption":["A spherically symmetric distribution of dust that leaves a singularity, comes to rest ($R_0 = 2\\,r_s$), and falls back, each point in the diagram a 2-sphere. Inside, the dust is a closed universe, $a^2(-d\\eta^2 + d\\chi^2 + \\sin^2\\chi\\,d\\Omega^2)$ with $a = a_m\\sin^2(\\eta/2)$, already conformal to the Einstein static universe, and it is drawn with $T = \\eta - \\pi$ and $X = \\chi$. Outside, $p = P(U)$ and $q = Q(V)$ are functions $P$ and $Q$ of the Kruskal coordinates $U$ and $V$, and three conditions fix them completely: the two sides agree on the surface $\\chi = \\chi_0$, a radial geodesic of the exterior with energy $\\cos\\chi_0$; the moment of rest is the line $T = 0$, the exterior's symmetry $t \\to -t$; and each singularity $r = 0$ is one line, $T = \\pm\\pi$.","The lower half is Oppenheimer and Snyder's collapse upside down. The past horizon $V = 0$ runs from $i^-$ into the dust and reaches the centre at $\\eta = 3\\chi_0$, after the surface has crossed $r_s$ at $\\eta = 2\\chi_0$, and no ray from $\\mathscr{I}^-$ arrives below it. Marginally trapped spheres run along $\\eta = 2\\chi$ in the lower half and $\\eta = 2\\pi - 2\\chi$ in the upper, timelike curves both, and the event horizon leaves the centre at $\\eta = 2\\pi - 3\\chi_0$ for $i^+$."],"layers":[{"kind":"fill","class":"region","points":[[0.7854,-3.1416],[0.7854,3.1416],[2.3562,3.1416],[5.4978,0.0],[2.3562,-3.1416]]},{"kind":"fill","class":"region","points":[[0.0,-3.1416],[0.7854,-3.1416],[0.7854,3.1416],[0.0,3.1416]]},{"kind":"fill","class":"star","points":[[0.0,-3.1416],[0.7854,-3.1416],[0.7854,3.1416],[0.0,3.1416]]},{"kind":"fill","class":"cover","points":[[0.7854,-3.1416],[0.7854,3.1416],[2.3562,3.1416],[5.4978,0.0],[2.3562,-3.1416]]},{"kind":"line","class":"t2","points":[[0.0,0.5],[0.7854,0.5]]},{"kind":"line","class":"t2","points":[[0.0,-0.5],[0.7854,-0.5]]},{"kind":"line","class":"t2","points":[[0.0,1.0],[0.7854,1.0]]},{"kind":"line","class":"t2","points":[[0.0,-1.0],[0.7854,-1.0]]},{"kind":"line","class":"t2","points":[[0.0,1.5],[0.7854,1.5]]},{"kind":"line","class":"t2","points":[[0.0,-1.5],[0.7854,-1.5]]},{"kind":"line","class":"t2","points":[[0.0,2.0],[0.7854,2.0]]},{"kind":"line","class":"t2","points":[[0.0,-2.0],[0.7854,-2.0]]},{"kind":"line","class":"t2","points":[[0.0,2.5],[0.7854,2.5]]},{"kind":"line","class":"t2","points":[[0.0,-2.5],[0.7854,-2.5]]},{"kind":"line","class":"t2","points":[[0.0,2.9],[0.7854,2.9]]},{"kind":"line","class":"t2","points":[[0.0,-2.9],[0.7854,-2.9]]},{"kind":"line","class":"t2","points":[[0.0,0.0],[0.7854,0.0]]},{"kind":"line","class":"r2","points":[[0.2618,-3.1416],[0.2618,3.1416]]},{"kind":"line","class":"r2","points":[[0.5236,-3.1416],[0.5236,3.1416]]},{"kind":"line","class":"r","points":[[0.92,2.4276],[1.5447,2